# Android Skills (Always Apply)

Before implementing, refactoring, or reviewing Android/Compose work, **read and follow the matching skill(s)**. Prefer skills over ad-hoc patterns.

## How to use

1. Identify the task domain (architecture, MVI, data, Compose UI, navigation, tests, etc.).
2. Open the listed skill `SKILL.md` and follow its conventions (naming, layering, checklist).
3. Do not invent conflicting patterns.

Skill roots:

- `C:\Users\user\.claude\skills\<name>\SKILL.md`
- `C:\Users\user\.agents\skills\<name>\SKILL.md`
- `C:\Users\user\.cursor\skills\<name>\SKILL.md`
- `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (project skills, shipped with this repo)

---

## Locked decisions

- **Skills:** Strict adherence — non-negotiable except approved deviations below.
- **DI: Koin only.** Never Hilt/Dagger. Follow `android-di-koin`.
- **Navigation: Navigation 3** (`navigation-3` skill). Not Nav2.
- **Offline-first:** Room/DataStore.
- **Modules:** Exactly 3 — `:app`, `:core:domain`, `:core:data`. Features are **packages under `:app`**, not `:feature:*` Gradle modules.
- **Motion:** Premium feel via `android-compose-animation`; pick the API first with `android-compose-motion-decisions` (project skill, from the team talk).
- **`android-architecture` override:** Use for Clean Architecture layers only; ignore Hilt.

### Approved deviations (only these)

| Skill | Deviation | Still follow |
|---|---|---|
| `android-module-structure` | Packages in `:app` / `:core:*` instead of `:feature:*` modules | Layer deps, version catalog, Koin, Room/DataStore |
| `android-architecture` | Ignore Hilt | Clean layers; presentation ≠ data impls |
| `android-navigation` | Use Navigation 3 | Type-safe keys; assemble in `:app` |
